/**
\page configuration Configuration

This page documents all configuration parameters that can be set in
`config.toml` (see `uvim --init-config`). The init command also copies
bundled themes into `~/.config/uvim/themes/`.

\section config_layout Layout

Configuration is a TOML document. Most editor settings use the canonical
`editor.*` keys, but for many options the parser also accepts
`settings.*` and a bare key without a prefix.

Boolean values accept: `true/false`, `1/0`, or `on/off`.

Example:
\code{.toml}
[editor]
tabspaces = 4
autobraces = true

[editor.status]
lspgap = 7

[editor.syntax.cpp]
semantic_tokens = true

[editor.filebrowser]
fuzzy = false

[theme.base]
fg = "#e0def4"
bg = "#1f1d2e"

[theme.syntax]
type = "#9ccfd8"
\endcode

\section config_examples Examples

\subsection config_examples_editor Editor example
\code{.toml}
[editor]
tabspaces = 2
autobraces = true
autoquotes = true
autobracesinstrings = true
splitbraces = true
autobrackets = true
splitbrackets = true
continuationindent = true
collectionindentwidth = 0
collectionindentkey = "ctrl-t"
asmdimunmapped = true
asmdocsapi = true
autotags = true
autocomplete = true
completionautoparens = true
usesystemclipboard = true
utf8 = true
showtabs = false
relativenumber = true
gitdefaultcolors = true
commenttogglepartial = false
formatoninsertleave = true
formatonsave = true
formatondoubleesctimeoutms = 300
rgupdate = 300
progressstyle = color
pickerstyle = float

[editor.picker]
width = 80
height = 70
preview = true
gdcenter = true
autodetectlsps = true

[editor.filebrowser]
fuzzy = false

[editor.commandline]
messageprefix = false

[editor.status]
lspgap = 7
\endcode

\subsection config_examples_syntax Syntax example
\code{.toml}
[editor.syntax]
json = true
yaml = true

[editor.syntax.robot]
keywords = "if, else, end"
highlight_titles = true
highlight_calls = true
custom_keywords = "My Keyword, Another One"
settings = "library, resource"

[editor.syntax.cpp]
highlight_members = true
highlight_type_names = true
highlight_implicit_members = true
highlight_param_types = true
highlight_system_includes = true
semantic_tokens = true

[editor.syntax.mlang]
semantic_tokens = true
highlight_types = true
highlight_builtin_docs = true
\endcode

\subsection config_examples_python Python formatting example
\code{.toml}
[editor.python]
formatter = "ruff"
\endcode

\subsection config_examples_theme Theme example
\code{.toml}
[theme.base]
fg = "#e0def4"
bg = "#1f1d2e"

[theme.ui]
accent = "#c4a7e7"
info = "#9ccfd8"

[theme.syntax]
type = "#9ccfd8"
function = "#6b86c9"
member = "#89dceb"
\endcode

\section config_editor Editor settings

\par editor.tabspaces
Integer. Default: 4. Tab width used by indent and display.

\par editor.autobraces
Boolean. Default: true. Auto-insert closing brace on `{([`.

\par editor.autoquotes
Boolean. Default: true. Auto-insert closing quote on `"`/`'`/`` ` ``.

\par editor.autobracesinstrings
Boolean. Default: true. Auto-insert `{}` and `[]` pairs inside strings.

\par editor.splitbraces
Boolean. Default: true. Enter between `{}` places the cursor on an indented
blank line and aligns the closing `}` with the leading whitespace of the opening
block. This preserves nested indentation, including tabs, and any text after `}`.
Use `:set splitbraces=false` (or `:set nosplitbraces`) for the previous single-line
split behavior. Use `:set splitbraces=true` to restore the default and
`:set splitbraces?` to query it. Persist this preference with `splitbraces = false`
in the `[editor]` section of the config file.

\par editor.autobrackets
Boolean. Default: true. Auto-insert `]` when typing `[`, skip an existing `]`
when typing it, and remove an empty `[]` pair with Backspace. Requires
`autobraces=true`; pairing in strings also requires `autobracesinstrings=true`.
Use `:set autobrackets=false` or `:set noautobrackets` to disable this behavior.

\par editor.splitbrackets
Boolean. Default: true. Enter inside `[]` creates an indented blank line and
aligns `]` with the opening line's leading whitespace, preserving trailing text.
This also works for manually inserted pairs and is independent of `splitbraces`.
Use `:set splitbrackets=false` or `:set nosplitbrackets` for a normal line split.
Both settings support `:set <name>?`, `:set <name>=true/false`, and config entries
under `[editor]`.

\par editor.continuationindent
Boolean. Default: true. On Enter, continue one indent level inside lists `[]`,
map/object literals `{}`, and argument lists `()`, including after an item or
comma. Strings and comments do not contribute delimiter nesting. Closing-only
lines align with their opening line; a line with an item followed by the closing
delimiter stays indented with the other items.
Use `:set continuationindent=false` to keep the preceding line's indentation.
This is independent of `splitbraces` and `splitbrackets`, which control empty pairs.

\par editor.collectionindentwidth
Integer. Default: 0. Range: 0-16. Width for collection continuation, empty-pair
expansion, and the reindent shortcut. Zero uses the buffer indent width
(`.clang-format` IndentWidth when available, otherwise `tabspaces`).
Example: `:set collectionindentwidth=2`.

\par editor.collectionindentkey
String. Default: "ctrl-t". Values: "ctrl-t", "ctrl-y", "off".
In Normal or Insert mode, Ctrl+T reindents the enclosing multiline list, map,
or argument list, including nested items, as one undoable edit. On its opening
line, the cursor may be before the opening delimiter. Only leading whitespace
changes; items, punctuation, line breaks, and comments remain intact. Multiline
string and block-comment contents are preserved. No formatter or LSP is needed.
The shortcut stays in the current mode and preserves the cursor's text position.
Example: `:set collectionindentkey=ctrl-y` to use Ctrl+Y instead, or
`:set collectionindentkey=off` to disable it. All three settings support queries
with `:set <name>?` and can be persisted in `[editor]`.

\par editor.asmdocsapi
Boolean. Default: true. Prefer cached/Compiler Explorer API instruction
information in the assembly inspection popup. The exact inspected instruction is
shown above the documentation; any API operand forms/examples precede fetch metadata. Fetching is asynchronous; built-in help stays visible until API content
arrives and remains the fallback when fetching fails. Row navigation restarts a
300 ms debounce before changing inspector content. Pending retrieval shows a
loading indicator only after another 300 ms; fast responses cancel it. Inspector
requests do not emit queue/download status messages.
Use `:set asmdocsapi=false` or `:set noasmdocsapi` for built-in help only,
`:set asmdocsapi` to enable API help, and `:set asmdocsapi?` to query the setting.
This controls assembly inspection independently of `--asm-docs-fetch` for `gd`.

\par editor.asmdimunmapped
Boolean. Default: true. In the assembly browser, dim labels, instructions, and
directives without direct source links while retaining their syntax colors.
Directly mapped instructions keep full brightness. Inferred source labels use
light dimming, external-source rows use medium dimming, and unknown origins use
the deepest shade. All unresolved rows are dimmed, including labels and directives. When debug information identifies the
origin of external code, the status bar shows its source filename and line.
Unidentified rows are marked as having no source mapping; no library is guessed.
If there is no source mapping at all, rows use the deepest shade.
Use `:set asmdimunmapped=false` or `:set noasmdimunmapped` to disable dimming,
`:set asmdimunmapped` to enable it, and `:set asmdimunmapped?` to query it.

\par editor.autotags
Boolean. Default: true. Auto-insert closing tags in markup.

\par editor.autocomplete
Boolean. Default: true. Enable auto-completion in insert mode.

\par editor.completionautoparens
Boolean. Default: true. Auto-insert parentheses after function completion.

\par editor.usesystemclipboard
Boolean. Default: true. Use the system clipboard for copy/paste.

\par editor.utf8
Boolean. Default: true. Enable UTF-8 handling.

\par editor.showtabs
Boolean. Default: true. Visualize tab characters.

\par editor.relativenumber
Boolean. Default: true. Show relative line numbers.

\par editor.gitdefaultcolors
Boolean. Default: true. Use default git blame colors.

\par editor.commenttogglepartial
Boolean. Default: false. Allow partial-line comment toggle.

\par editor.formatoninsertleave
Boolean. Default: true. Format buffer on insert-mode exit.

\par editor.formatonsave
Boolean. Default: true. Format buffer on save.

\par editor.formatondoubleesctimeoutms
Integer. Default: 300. Range: 1-5000. Timeout (ms) for double-ESC format.

\par editor.rgupdate
Integer. Default: 300. Range: 0-5000. Delay (ms) before grep search updates
after typing in the `Ctrl-a` grep view. Use 0 for immediate updates.

\par editor.progressstyle
String. Default: color. One of `ascii` (`[=====.....]`), `glyph`
(eighth-block bar `▕████▌     ▏`) or `color` (glyph bar drawn with the
`theme.progress.fg`/`theme.progress.bg` colours). Style of the background
task progress shown in the status bar and the `:tasks` view. Non-UTF-8
terminals always use `ascii`.

\par editor.pickerstyle
String. Default: float. `float` opens the `Ctrl-p` file finder and the
`Ctrl-a` grep as a bordered floating window over the code (Telescope style)
with a preview pane when the window is wide enough; `fullscreen` uses the
classic fullscreen views. Narrow terminals fall back to fullscreen.

\par editor.picker.width
Integer. Default: 80. Range: 10-100. Floating picker width in percent of the
terminal.

\par editor.picker.height
Integer. Default: 70. Range: 10-100. Floating picker height in percent of the
terminal.

\par editor.picker.preview
Boolean. Default: true. Show the preview pane in floating pickers (file head
for `Ctrl-p`, the matched line in context for `Ctrl-a`). `Ctrl-v` toggles it
while a picker is open.

\par editor.gdcenter
Boolean. Default: true. Center screen on `gd` navigation.

\par editor.autodetectlsps
Boolean. Default: true. Auto-detect available LSP servers.
When uvim starts directly into a directory browser (for example `uvim .`),
auto-detected LSP startup is deferred until a file is opened.

\par editor.emitlsp
Boolean. Default: true. Store and display LSP-emitted diagnostics from
`textDocument/publishDiagnostics`. Set false to hide warning/error row markers
and disable the `Space-e` diagnostic popup while keeping other LSP features
available.

\par editor.filebrowser.fuzzy
Boolean. Default: false. Enable fuzzy search in file browser.

\par editor.status.lspgap
Integer. Default: 7. Range: 0-20. Padding between LSP label and line/column.

\par editor.commandline.messageprefix
Boolean. Default: false. Show `: ` prefix before status/loc/blame messages.

\section config_syntax Syntax highlighting

\par editor.syntax.json
Boolean. Default: true. Enable JSON highlighting.

\par editor.syntax.yaml
Boolean. Default: true. Enable YAML highlighting.

\par editor.syntax.robot.keywords
String (CSV). Default: list from default config. Set to `none` or `false`
to disable.

\par editor.syntax.robot.highlight_titles
Boolean. Default: true. Highlight Robot section headers.

\par editor.syntax.robot.highlight_calls
Boolean. Default: true. Highlight Robot keyword calls.

\par editor.syntax.robot.custom_keywords
String (CSV). Default: empty. Custom Robot keywords to highlight.

\par editor.syntax.robot.settings
String (CSV). Default: list from default config. Robot settings to highlight.

\par editor.syntax.cpp.highlight_members
Boolean. Default: true. Highlight member accesses.

\par editor.syntax.cpp.highlight_type_names
Boolean. Default: true. Highlight type names.

\par editor.syntax.cpp.highlight_implicit_members
Boolean. Default: true. Highlight implicit member references.

\par editor.syntax.cpp.highlight_param_types
Boolean. Default: true. Highlight parameter types in signatures.

\par editor.syntax.cpp.highlight_system_includes
Boolean. Default: true. Highlight system include headers.

\par editor.syntax.cpp.semantic_tokens
Boolean. Default: true. Use clangd semantic tokens for C++ types.

\par editor.syntax.cpp.locals_color
Token name. Default: `normal`. Color used for local variables and parameters.
Valid values: `normal`, `keyword`, `type`, `string`, `char`, `comment`,
`preprocessor`, `number`, `operator`, `function`, `member`.

\par editor.syntax.cpp.member_color
Token name. Default: `member`. Color used for C++ members (fields/accesses).
Valid values: `normal`, `keyword`, `type`, `string`, `char`, `comment`,
`preprocessor`, `number`, `operator`, `function`, `member`.

\par editor.syntax.mlang.highlight_types
Boolean. Default: true. Highlight Mlang types.

\par editor.syntax.mlang.semantic_tokens
Boolean. Default: true. Use Mlang LSP semantic tokens for keywords, types,
functions, and related symbols. Requires Mlang LSP support.

\par editor.syntax.mlang.highlight_builtin_docs
Boolean. Default: true. Highlight Mlang builtin docs.

\section config_python Python formatting

\par editor.python.formatter
String. Default: `ruff`. Supported values: `ruff`, `black`.

\section config_theme Theme

Theme colors accept hex RGB strings like `"#RRGGBB"`.

\par theme.name
String. When set, load a theme from `~/.config/uvim/themes/<name>.toml`
(`$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/uvim/themes/` if set). If the name has no extension,
`.toml` is appended.

\par theme.file
String. Absolute or relative path to a theme TOML file to load.

\par theme.path
Alias for `theme.file`.

\par theme.base.fg
Default: `#e0def4`. Base foreground.

\par theme.base.bg
Default: `#1f1d2e`. Base background.

\par theme.base.foreground
Alias for `theme.base.fg`.

\par theme.base.background
Alias for `theme.base.bg`.

\par theme.debugger.source_bg / variables_bg / threads_bg / execution_bg
Optional background colors for debugger source, variables, threads, and the
execution line. Defaults derive from the base background and theme accents.
Alternating rows receive an additional tint, syntax foreground colors are
preserved, and the focused selection uses `theme.selection`. Set these keys
under `[theme.debugger]`, for example `variables_bg = "#2e3335"`.

\par theme.asm.selection_bg
Background color for the source range used to filter a visual-selection assembly
view. Defaults to a muted blue tint derived from the editor background. The tint
stays on the selected range while browsing; the currently linked source line uses
the green mapping highlight and the active cursor keeps its usual highlight.
Syntax foreground colors are preserved. Example: `selection_bg = "#28354e"`
under `[theme.asm]`. Applies to the source pane of `:asm . --split`.

\par theme.asm.external_bg
Color. Default: a subtle dark red blended with the theme base background.
Background for assembly rows whose compiler-provided origin is an external
source file, including standard-library code. Syntax colors and dimming remain
visible. Source-linked highlighting and the active row's selection take priority.
Unknown origins keep their usual background. This tint is independent of
`editor.asmdimunmapped`. Example: `external_bg = "#351c26"` under `[theme.asm]`.

\par theme.ui.dim
Default: `#6e6a86`.

\par theme.ui.accent
Default: `#c4a7e7`.

\par theme.ui.info
Default: `#9ccfd8`.

\par theme.ui.warning
Default: `#f6c177`.

\par theme.ui.success
Default: `#9ece6a`.

\par theme.ui.error
Default: `#eb6f92`.

\par theme.ui.directory
Default: `#3e8fb0`.

\par theme.ui.gutter
Default: `#3e8fb0`.

\par theme.ui.prompt
Default: `#9ece6a`.

\par theme.statusline.fg
Default: `#e0def4`.

\par theme.statusline.bg
Default: `#26233a`.

\par theme.tabbar.fg
Default: `#e0def4`.

\par theme.tabbar.bg
Default: `#2a273f`.

\par theme.selection.fg
Default: `#e0def4`.

\par theme.selection.bg
Default: `#403d52`.

\par theme.cursor.fg
Default: `#1f1d2e`.

\par theme.cursor.bg
Default: `#f6c177`.

\par theme.search.fg
Default: `#1f1d2e`.

\par theme.search.bg
Default: `#ebbcba`.

\par theme.panel.fg
Default: `#e0def4`.

\par theme.panel.bg
Default: `#2a283e`.

\par theme.syntax.normal
Default: `#e0def4`.

\par theme.syntax.keyword
Default: `#c4a7e7`.

\par theme.syntax.type
Default: `#9ccfd8`.

\par theme.syntax.string
Default: `#9ece6a`.

\par theme.syntax.char
Default: `#9ece6a`.

\par theme.syntax.comment
Default: `#6e6a86`.

\par theme.syntax.preprocessor
Default: `#f6c177`.

\par theme.syntax.number
Default: `#eb6f92`.

\par theme.syntax.operator
Default: `#f6c177`.

\par theme.syntax.function
Default: `#6b86c9`.

\par theme.syntax.member
Default: `#89dceb`.
Configure this separately to make members lighter/darker than functions.

\par theme.syntax.namespace1
Default: `#9b7fbf`. First and darkest qualified namespace segment.

\par theme.syntax.namespace2
Default: `#aa8dce`. Intermediate qualified namespace segment.

\par theme.syntax.namespace3
Default: `#b79adc`. Brighter qualified namespace segment.

\par theme.syntax.namespace4
Default: `#c4a7e7`. Final and brightest qualified namespace segment.

*/
